<title>JAPAN: S&amp;P assigns BBB to Fuji Finance preference shares.</title>
<headline>S&amp;P assigns BBB to Fuji Finance preference shares.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Standard &amp; Poor's Corp said on Monday it had assigned a BBB rating to Fuji Finance (Bermuda) Trust's 210 billion yen worth of preference shares, which represent an interest in noncumulative mandatory convertible preference shares issued by Fuji Bank Ltd.</p>
<p>S&amp;P said in a statement that the rating reflected the creditworthiness of preferred shares issued by Fuji Bank.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Treasury Desk +81-3-5473-3748</p>
</text>
